From cb8b3e93543bdd8e8f14507134d681fba06584d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:43:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: surround as Dolby for a display that takes only
 stereo PCM

An LG C5 declares, on some starts, its own audio: PCM in 2 channels, AC-3
in 6 and E-AC-3 in 8, no speaker allocation (2026-10-15 and 2026-10-21).
Its sound bar on eARC took what the TV passed on: TrueHD Atmos passed
through played on the bar. A DTS track, which the TV does not take, was
decoded, and since "AudioEngine: PCM in no more channels than the display
takes" it was mixed down to stereo: with a 7.1.4 bar, the film came out
in stereo.

Kodi can already encode decoded multichannel sound to Dolby Digital
(Plus) 5.1 and pass it through, "Enable Dolby Digital transcoding"
(audiooutput.ac3transcode, off by default), but only where "Number of
channels" is 2.0, and the setting is shown only then: with the setting
at 7.1 and the channels limited to the display, it could not be had.

Now, where "Number of channels" asks for more than 2.0, the display of
the output takes PCM in 2 channels at most (its audio data, as limited
by LimitChannelsToDisplay(), the kept ones in a change of mode
included), and the display of the passthrough output declares Dolby in
more than 2 channels, a multichannel track that Kodi decodes is encoded
and passed through, as that transcoding does (MODE_TRANSCODE in
ApplySettingsToFormat()): to Dolby Digital Plus 5.1 where the display
declares it in more than 2 channels and its passthrough is on, else to
Dolby Digital 5.1 where the display declares that in more than 2. The
rule is AE::PCM::DolbyForStereoDisplay(); the ELD parser now also keeps
the channels of Dolby Digital and Dolby Digital Plus of the display
(CAEDeviceInfo::m_maxAc3Channels, m_maxEac3Channels, in the list of
outputs as "m_maxDolby").

A setting, "Surround as Dolby when the display takes only stereo PCM"
(audiooutput.hadessurroundtodolby, System > Audio, under "Dolby Digital
(AC3) capable receiver", Advanced level, shown where "Number of
channels" is above 2.0 and the limit to the display is on), on by
default, turns it off: the track is then mixed down to stereo PCM, as
before. Its help says the cost: the encoding is lossy (Kodi's rates:
768 kb/s for Dolby Digital Plus, 640 kb/s for Dolby Digital), and 7.1
is mixed to 5.1.

Nothing changes:
- where the display takes the channels of the setting in PCM (the same
  TV on the days it declared the bar's 8 channels; any receiver);
- for "Number of channels" at 2.0, where "Enable Dolby Digital
  transcoding" stays the setting, as Kodi has it; when that is on, its
  own choice of format is kept;
- for stereo tracks, GUI sounds, and stereo upmix;
- for passthrough of the track itself.

Fail closed: passthrough or Dolby Digital passthrough off, no Dolby
declared in more than 2 channels, or no encoder that opens (each
encoder is opened once, 5.1 at 48 kHz in planar float as the transcode
asks it; an E-AC-3 encoder that is not there and falls back to AC-3
inside CAEEncoderFFmpeg does not count), and the track is mixed down to
stereo as before. Should the encoder not open when the sink is
configured all the same, the engine is configured again with PCM rather
than sending nothing (Kodi ignored the result of Initialize() there).
The log says once what is done and why ("multichannel tracks that Kodi
decodes go out encoded to Dolby Digital Plus 5.1 and passed through",
or which of the reasons left them in stereo).

Checked on the host: FFmpeg 9.0.2, built from the verified source of the
image with its AC-3 and E-AC-3 encoders, encodes a 5.1 channel test
(each channel alone, in turn) at 768 kb/s E-AC-3 and 640 kb/s AC-3 to
5.1(side); decoded, each channel is in its own place, the loudest other
channel 83 dB or more below it, and the LFE kept. LibreELEC builds
FFmpeg with both encoders (--enable-encoder=ac3, eac3).

Host tests (TestAEPcmChannels): the Dolby of the ELDs of the reports;
the choice for that TV (E-AC-3), its passthrough off (AC-3), a display
of AC-3 or E-AC-3 only, encoders that do not open, the setting off,
passthrough off, no Dolby, and every case where nothing changes; and
the same choice through a change of mode. Eleven mutations of the rules
make them fail. Not run on the host: the engine (compiled, and read).

The strings are core strings in English (39882, 39883), translated in
Estuary (32112, 32113: es_es, es_ar, es_mx).
